      "worked": "At $x=1$:\n\n$$\\begin{align*}f(1)&=1^2-1\\\\f(1)&=0\\\\f_L(1)&=2(1)+k\\\\f_L(1)&=2+k\\\\f_R(1)&=1^2-1\\\\f_R(1)&=0\\end{align*}$$\n\nContinuity requires all three values to agree:\n\n$$\\begin{align*}2+k&=0\\\\k&=-2\\end{align*}$$\n\nBoth polynomial branches are continuous on their intervals. With $k=-2$, they also match at $x=1$, so $f$ is continuous throughout its domain.",
